    "memory:memory/2026-04-18.md:18:23": {
      "key": "memory:memory/2026-04-18.md:18:23",
      "path": "memory/2026-04-18.md",
      "startLine": 18,
      "endLine": 23,
      "source": "memory",
      "snippet": "- New issue discovered: every Telegram reply triggered permission card `mcp__plugin_telegram_telegram__reply`. - Added Telegram MCP tools to Paganel Claude allowlist/settings (reply, react, edit_message, download_attachment) and restarted, but Telegram permission cards still appeared. - Tried `--permission-mode dontAsk` with user approval; result was worse: Paganel stopped replying entirely. - Logs showed concrete failure: in `don't ask` mode, Claude denied `mcp__plugin_telegram_telegram__reply` because the tool was blocked by runtime permissions. - Current best next step (not yet applied before compaction): remove `--permission-mode dontAsk`, launch Paganel with explicit `--allowedTools` in",
